        12: `Verse 1  
In the days of old, when the walls stood tall,  
Zerubbabel led, with a heart for the call.  
Priests and Levites, united in grace,  
Gathered in Jerusalem, to seek God’s face.  

Chorus  
Lift your voices, let the praises rise,  
With thanksgiving, we behold the skies.  
For the joy of the Lord fills this sacred place,  
Songs of the redeemed, we sing of His grace.  

Verse 2  
From the fields of Geba to the plains of song,  
The Levites rejoiced, where our hearts belong.  
Jeshua and Ezra, with instruments in hand,  
Together we stand, in this promised land.  

Chorus  
Lift your voices, let the praises rise,  
With thanksgiving, we behold the skies.  
For the joy of the Lord fills this sacred place,  
Songs of the redeemed, we sing of His grace.  

Bridge  
Purify our hearts, O Lord, we pray,  
As we walk in Your light, guide us each day.  
With every trumpet, every cymbal's sound,  
In His presence, our hope is found.  

Verse 3  
Great sacrifices offered, with joy they came,  
Families rejoicing, lifting His name.  
From the towers to gates, we proclaim His might,  
In unity, we stand, in the warmth of His light.  

Chorus  
Lift your voices, let the praises rise,  
With thanksgiving, we behold the skies.  
For the joy of the Lord fills this sacred place,  
Songs of the redeemed, we sing of His grace.  

Outro  
So let the joy of Jerusalem be heard afar,  
In the heart of His people, shines our morning star.  
Together we sing, forever we'll praise,  
In the songs of the redeemed, our hearts ablaze.`,
        13: `[TITLE] Remember Me, O My God

[Verse 1]  
In the shadow of Your temple, Lord,  
We gather as Your faithful ones,  
With hearts laid bare, we seek Your Word,  
In brokenness, our journey runs.  
The ones who turned from You, we mourn,  
The blessings turned to bitter strife,  
Yet even in their curse, we learn,  
You turn our trials into life.  

[Chorus]  
Remember me, O my God,  
For the deeds of my heart, I cry,  
In the chambers of Your love,  
Let not my labor pass You by.  
Oh, cleanse us from all that defiles,  
Restore the joy of holy days,  
In reverence, we seek Your face,  
Remember me, O God, always.  

[Verse 2]  
The Sabbath rests, a holy sign,  
Yet burdens brought upon the day,  
I call to those who tread the line,  
To guard this gift, to walk Your way.  
With every vow and every plea,  
We rise to cast the wrong aside,  
For in Your grace, we’re truly free,  
Our hearts, in You, are unified.  

[Chorus]  
Remember me, O my God,  
For the deeds of my heart, I cry,  
In the chambers of Your love,  
Let not my labor pass You by.  
Oh, cleanse us from all that defiles,  
Restore the joy of holy days,  
In reverence, we seek Your face,  
Remember me, O God, always.  

[Bridge]  
From ashes, You bring forth our song,  
In unity, we stand as one,  
With faithful hearts, we will be strong,  
For every battle, You have won.  
Though we may falter, still we rise,  
In Your embrace, we find our fight,  
Through every tear, our spirits fly,  
In Your great mercy, we find light.  

[Chorus]  
Remember me, O my God,  
For the deeds of my heart, I cry,  
In the chambers of Your love,  
Let not my labor pass You by.  
Oh, cleanse us from all that defiles,  
Restore the joy of holy days,  
In reverence, we seek Your face,  
Remember me, O God, always.  

[Outro]  
Remember me, O my God,  
In all my ways, I seek Your grace,  
With every breath, my heart beats loud,  
Forever in Your holy place.  
Remember me, O God, always.`,
